    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1025">

                <pb facs="0895" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/16986.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Simpich</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-21T22:00:00-07:23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1915—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 21. General Obregon is authorized to proceed to El Paso via
                    American Territory, provided he travels as civilian and unarmed. So inform
                    federal authorities on border, especially military authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
